    "content": "{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_3434a55fd88f0c468520363b9c207866\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://platform.tracxn.com/a/d/company/5c49cd448f08a3a26dc14bb0/capsida?utm_source=parallel&utm_medium=ai#a:about\",\n      \"title\": \"Capsida\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Name: Capsida | Website Url: http://capsida.com | Primary Sector: Life Sciences | Primary Subsector: Gene Therapy | Stage: Series A | Founded Year: 2019 | Employee Count Official: 54 | Location Country: United States | Location State: California | Location City: Newbury Park | Latest Funding Round Amount Usd: 50000000.0 | Latest Funding Round Date: 2021-04-29 | Latest Funding Round Name: Series A | Total Disclosed Funding Usd: 50000000.0 | Acquisitions As Acquirer Count: 0 | Funded: Yes | Has Female Founder: Yes | Other Taxonomy Tags: [\\\"US Tech\\\",\\\"Enterprise Tech - US\\\",\\\"Life Sciences -\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/Nick_Goeden_1445_May-14_Theater-C_Identification-of-Multiple-BBB-Receptors.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"PowerPoint Presentation\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"**Clinical trial start-up activities have initiated for CAP-002** Characteristic Industry Standard AAV9 Capsida Lead Capsid Productivity in crude lysate 1E11 vg/ml 6.2E11 vg/ml Packaging (Empty/Full) >70% ~90% Aggregation < 10% 5% Overall Recovery ~25% 36% 13 13 **Identification of Distinct Novel Receptors with High Cross-Species Conservation Significantly De-Risks Clinical Translatability** _NR001 NR002 NR003 NR004 NR005_ _Novel Capsid_ _A_ _Novel Capsid_ _B_ _Novel Capsid_ _C_ _Novel Capsid_ _D_ _Novel Capsid_ _E_ NHP 96% 99% 96% 98% 93% Sequence Identity to Human _\\\\*Sequence identity is calculated across full protein and is not restricted to predicted binding site_ **Capsida Biotherapeutics has successfully filed patents for all five of these groundbreaking** **novel receptors and is focused on further expanding the IP portfolio surrounding them** 14 14 **The predictive power of in vitro receptor binding is confirmed by AAV transduction** **in cell lines with receptor expression** _Binding also confirmed for NR002-5_ **Bead-Based Receptor Binding Detection Plate-Based Receptor Binding Detection** _Human and NHP ortholog binding confirmed_ **In Vitro Binding Platform Demonstrates Reproducible Capsid/Receptor Binding Data Consistent with Expression Profiles** 15 15 **Novel Receptors Highly Expressed in Neurons and Brain Endothelial Cells Enable More Specific Delivery to the CNS** • **Improved safety profile** • Lower expression in off-target cell types relative to TfR • **Differentiated CNS delivery mechanisms** • NR004: endothelial-specific\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.capsida.com/pipeline\",\n      \"title\": \"Capsida Biotherapeutics - Engineering novel AAVs and developing the next generation of gene therapies\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2014-12-30\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"UNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL\\nAbout\\nCapsida Biotherapeutics is developing next generation, targeted genetic medicines for rare and more common neurological and ocular diseases across all ages.\\nAbout\\nInnovation\\nScience & Innovation\\nTHE CAPSIDA APPROACH\\nUNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL\\nCapsida integrates all capabilities needed to surpass the challenges of gene therapy.\\ngraphic\\nCapsid Engineering and Preclinical\\nUNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL\\nAt Capsida, the scale at which we have engineered capsids is unrivaled.\\nUNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL\\nCapsida’s founding technology originated in the lab of Caltech’s Viviana Gradinaru, Ph.D., Professor of Neurosciences and Biological Engineering at the Tianqiao and Chrissy Chen Institute of Neuroscience.\\nUNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL\\nFounded in 2019, Capsida is financed by Versant Ventures and Westlake Village BioPartners and has entered into strategic collaborations with AbbVie, CRISPR Therapeutics, and Lilly’s Gene Therapy Division.\\nUNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL > CAPSIDA NEWS & EVENTS\\nMay 12, 2026\\nCapsida to Present Preclinical Data of New Next-Generation, High-Performing Ocular Capsids at ASGCT Annual Meeting\\nProvides corporate update including appointment of gene therapy expert Romuald Corbau, Ph.D., as Chief Scientific Officer and an update on the CNS programs…\\nMay 11, 2026\\nUNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL > CAPSIDA NEWS & EVENTS\\nCAP-002 Program Update: A Letter to the STXBP1 Community\\nSEE ALL NEWS & EVENTS >\\nCapsida Logo\\ninfo@capsida.com 1300 Rancho Conejo Blvd. Thousand Oaks, CA 91320\\n© 2026 Capsida Biotherapeutics ® . All rights reserved – Privacy Policy | Terms of Use\\nPrivacy Preference Center\\nPrivacy Preferences\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/Capsida_Mar_2025_Corp_Deck.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"[PDF] Capsida Biotherapeutics\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2025-03-07\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Solving the Challenges of Gen-1 Genetic Medicines\\nStarting in CNS and Ophthalmology with IP rights and applicability across all therapeutic areas\\nCapsida Solutions CNS Challenges\\nCrossing the BBB\\nLimited ability to cross BBB; < 1% neuronal transduction >70% of neurons transduced in NHPs\\n» Protected by expansive IP\\nportfolio\\nCAP-002: STXBP1-DEE\\nCAP-004: FA\\nCAP-003: PD-GBA • Human POC in Q4\\nTwo clinical programs in 2025\\nThird clinical program in 2026\\nWholly-owned Programs with Multiple Catalysts in 2025\\ninfo@capsida.com\\n1300 Rancho Conejo Blvd Thousand Oaks, California\\nwww.capsida.com\\nOur Pipeline is Making the Impossible Possible\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12816303\",\n      \"title\": \"Strategies of AAV capsid engineering for targeted delivery to brain, muscle, and retina\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2026-01-06\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"For CNS applications, receptor-informed engineering—such as capsids targeting transferrin receptor 1 (TfR1) or alkaline phosphatase (ALPL)—has produced large gains in blood–brain barrier (BBB) penetration and cross-species translation.\\n2 Capsid engineering to improve delivery\\n2.1 CNS: species-dependent differences in blood-brain barrier (BBB) receptor usage and AAV tropism\\nVoyager used receptor-mapping to show that alkaline phosphatase (ALPL) is the primary receptor for its cross-species BBB capsid VCAP-102 (Moyer et al., 2025), with direct binding to human ALPL sufficient to drive receptor-mediated transcytosis in barrier models—an instructive template for mechanistically anchored translation.\\nA complementary path flips the problem: start with a known human BBB receptor and build binding into the capsid. The leading example is transferrin receptor 1 (TfR1/CD71).\\nSimilar logic underpins loop grafts/peptide displays to create receptor-targeted capsids (e.g., TfR1 binders for the BBB) and charge/geometry tuning at heparan-binding sites to enable ILM traversal after IVT.\\nIn addition, Fit4Function (Eid et al., 2024) formalized multi-trait optimization, training on multiplexed assays to predict sequences that simultaneously meet potency and developability constraints, with experimental validation across assays/species.\\nDesign and characterization of a novel intravitreal dual-transgene genetic medicine for neovascular retinopathies. Invest Ophthalmol. Vis. Sci. 65, 1. DOI: 10.1167/iovs.65.14.1 PMID: 39620832 PMCID: PMC11614000\\n15. Capsida (2021). Capsida biotherapeutics debuts with $140 million of capital.\\nAvailable online at: https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/capsida-biotherapeutics-debuts-with-140-million-of-capital-301279506.html (Accessed September 22, 2025).\\n16. Capsida Biotherapeutics (2025). A letter to the STXBP1 community. Available online at: https://capsida.com/a-letter-to-the-stxbp1-community/ (Accessed September 17, 2025).\\n17.\\nTargeting AAV vectors to the central nervous system by engineering capsids to bind defined BBB receptors. PLoS Biol. 21 (8), e3002112. DOI: 10.1371/journal.pbio.3002112 PMID: 37467291 PMCID: PMC10355383\\n46. Huang Q. Chan K. Y. Wu J. Botticello-Romero N. R. Zheng Q. Lou S. (2024).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/Capsida-Apr_2025_Corp_Deck_v1.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"PowerPoint Presentation\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2025-04-23\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Solving the Challenges of Gen-1 Genetic Medicines\\nStarting in CNS and Ophthalmology with IP rights and applicability across all therapeutic areas\\nCapsida Solutions CNS Challenges\\nCrossing the BBB\\nLimited ability to cross BBB; < 1% neuronal transduction >70% of neurons transduced in NHPs\\nExpression in NHPs with potential for full disease correction\\nIndustry leading expression levels across pipeline programs\\n26\\nIn-house Process & Analytical Development and cGMP Manufacturing\\nEnables Capsida to control quality, timelines, and costs\\nVector Production Rapid production of engineered capsids for preclinical studies\\n» Protected by expansive IP\\nportfolio\\nCAP-002: STXBP1-DEE\\nCAP-004: FA\\nCAP-003: PD-GBA • Human POC in Q4\\nTwo clinical programs in 2025\\nThird clinical program in 2026\\nWholly-owned Programs with Multiple Catalysts in 2025\\ninfo@capsida.com\\n1300 Rancho Conejo Blvd Thousand Oaks, California\\nwww.capsida.com\\nOur Pipeline is Making the Impossible Possible\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.the-scientist.com/a-journey-into-the-brain-71735\",\n      \"title\": \"A Journey Into the Brain | The Scientist\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2024-03-22\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"In the early 2010s, Deverman joined Gradinaru’s team at Caltech as a postdoctoral researcher, where he developed a pipeline to create and test novel AAV.\\nBefore these findings, they weren’t sure whether they had engineered a capsid that used the same receptor as AAV9, but just used it better, or whether they engineered a capsid that could bind a completely different receptor.\\nLY6A’s discovery suggested to them that they could test the ability of an engineered AAV to bind specific known proteins prior to graduating the capsids to time-consuming and costly in vivo experiments.\\nDeverman and his team recently transformed that idea into a high-throughput protein assay .\\nIn a recent preprint posted on bioRxiv , Deverman and his team reported using their receptor-targeting in vitro screen to discover AAV variants that bind the human transferrin receptor , a protein expressed on the BBB. 24\\nIn the next five to seven years, we'll really see the application of these come to fruition,” said Davidson.\\nViviana Gradinaru is a cofounder and board member of Capsida Biotherapeutics and has a patent for her AAV engineering research described in this story.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://platform.tracxn.com/a/d/company/56dfab09e4b0d470832c828a/capella%20bioscience?utm_source=parallel&utm_medium=ai#a:about\",\n      \"title\": \"Capella Bioscience\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Name: Capella Bioscience | Website Url: http://www.capellabioscience.com/ | Primary Sector: Life Sciences | Primary Subsector: Immunotherapy | Stage: Series A | Founded Year: 2014 | Employee Count Official: 3 | Location Country: United Kingdom | Location State: England | Location City: London | Latest Funding Round Amount Usd: 4850647.821 | Latest Funding Round Date: 2018-01-19 | Latest Funding Round Name: Series A | Latest Valuation Usd: 14269528.0 | Total Disclosed Funding Usd: 22814987.821000002 | Acquisitions As Acquirer Count: 0 | Funded: Yes | Other Taxonomy Tags: [\\\"Trending Themes in\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://capsida.com/publications\",\n      \"title\": \"Publications - Capsida Biotherapeutics\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2023-06-08\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Powered by Cookieyes logo\\nCapsida Logo\\n* About\\n* Overview\\n* Leadership Team\\n* Board of Directors\\n* Investors\\n* History\\n* Contact\\n* Innovation\\n* Capsida Approach\\n* CNS\\n* Ophthalmology\\n* Capsid Engineering and Preclinical\\n* News\\n* Press Releases\\n* Community Updates\\n* Publications\\n* Careers\\n* Culture & Benefits\\n* Current Opportunities\\nIdentification of Multiple Novel Blood-Brain-Barrier Receptors for CNS Gene Therapy and Other Drug Modalities via an Integrated AAV Capsid Engineering Platform – Download PDF\\nChuapoco, Flytzanis, Goeden et al biorxiv, January 2022\\nLink to view\\nCapsida Logo\\ninfo@capsida.com 1300 Rancho Conejo Blvd. Thousand Oaks, CA 91320\\n© 2026 Capsida Biotherapeutics ® . All rights reserved – Privacy Policy | Terms of Use\\nPrivacy Preference Center\\nPrivacy Preferences\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_ea3641f24ffeIOZGZcPjtin4s1\"\n}"
