    "content": "{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_09a6a6b1afb9e4c7f46e676371e647d9\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lirtx.com/post/starfish-fast-capsid-structure-generation\",\n      \"title\": \"Starfish: Fast Capsid Structure Generation\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Lir is building nAAVigator ® , a holistic AI pipeline to engineer viral vectors for gene therapy. It’s the in silico engine driving our lab-in-the-loop platform. We believe nAAVigator ® is the path towards creating smarter, safer, more effective medicines.\\nStarfish™ is an AI and physics-based structure generation pipeline enabling fast, accurate and physically plausible capsid structure generation capable of large library screening tasks. Capsids are large, complex multimers which are poorly supported by the current generation of protein folding algorithms.\\nStarfish™ rapidly identifies relevant binding surfaces for capsid multimers using cost-efficient hardware, enabling Lir to incorporate essential capsid structural analysis into large-scale viral variant library screenings.\\n‍\\n‍\\nThe first stage of our pipeline involves applying a protein folding model to generate the monomers involved in the capsid surface. This is followed by fast physics-based assembly and refinement algorithms.\\nOur method scales far better than multimer cofolding both in terms of runtime and compute requirements, with Starfish™ able to assemble the full capsid at acceptable runtimes for screening tens of thousands of variants.\\nOur approach resolves unrealistic clashes often produced by AI-generated structures, while anchoring the resulting complex in physics-based models suitable for downstream tasks such as molecular docking.\\n‍\\nAll approaches predict monomers and trimers accurately (RMSD <1Å) for wild-type proteins.\\nAlphafold2/Openfold scales poorly as the complexity of the surface portion increases, requiring over an hour to generate the 5-fold axis . Boltz2 is able to generate structures of the 3-fold axis in reasonable time but fails to generate a 5-fold axis, running out of memory (OOM) on a H100 80GB GPU.\\nStarfish™ remains accurate and faster up to the full capsid with less compute.\\n‍\\nWe built Starfish™ because existing models like Boltz2 and Alphafold aren’t capable of modelling whole viruses at the throughput we need.\\nViral capsids are made up of multiple overlapping proteins that form the surface of the virus. Much of Lir's work involves mutating the surface of capsids to alter the properties of viruses for gene therapy.\\nComputing large portions of the capsid using models such as Alphafold or Boltz2 is impractical when scaling to a large number of targets due to both their time and memory requirements.\\nOwing to its structural homogeneity, modelling the complete 60-mer AAV capsid is usually unnecessary, but portions of the surface such as at the 2, 3 and 5-fold axes are the minimum subunit for useful docking or structural assessment of capsid stability in silico .\\nStarfish™ is one part of Lir's nAAVigator ® pipeline which is designed to accelerate viral vector design. Combined with our lab-in-the-loop, we’re building a platform to generate vectors specific to clinical partners’ targets at speed. We'll continue to post development updates here in the coming months.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lirtx.com/blog\",\n      \"title\": \"Blog\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Read More Starfish: Fast Capsid Structure Generation February 4, 2026 Starfish is an AI and physics-based structure generation pipeline enabling fast, accurate and physically plausible capsid structure generation capable of large library screening tasks. It is allowing us to run docking and structural analysis tasks at scale as part of nAAVigator. Read More LirEvolve: Viral DNA Foundation Modelling December 18, 2025 LirEvolve is a viral foundation model which is already state-of-the-art in predicting the viability of novel viral vector designs. It is currently being improved further with our own in-house data, with the continued goal of a broadly applicable toolkit for viral vector evolution. This model is allowing Lir to accelerate the work in our lab already. It enables us to run more efficient experiments and focus on generating high quality datasets in every experimental run.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lirtx.com/\",\n      \"title\": \"Lir Therapeutics\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Pre-existing immunity to viral vectors excludes patients from accessing gene therapies. One of our core outputs is designing vectors to evade antibodies.\\nMaking AAV, better\\nLir’s first mission is AAV, the most widely used viral vector in gene therapy. Our goal is to unlock AAV’s true potential by remapping the surface of the capsid.\\nWith our ground up AI approach and high-throughput dataset generation pipeline, we're designing viruses never seen before.\\nAI-powered Virus Design\\nwith nAAVigator®\\nLir is decoding viral vectors. nAAVigator® is a holistic viral design engine trained on our unique datasets. It's been engineered to model viral vectors at all levels.\\nThe result: engineering for safety and efficacy simultaneously.\\nImmunogenicity\\nLandscape Models\\nPhysics-based\\nStructural Models\\nFunctional\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/spacetx/starfish\",\n      \"title\": \"GitHub - spacetx/starfish: starfish: unified pipelines for image-based transcriptomics · GitHub\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"It lets you build scalable pipelines that localize and quantify RNA transcripts in image data generated by any FISH method, from simple RNA single-molecule FISH to combinatorial barcoded assays.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://pharmasource.global/content/news/cdmo-news/vectorbuilder-partners-with-lir-therapeutics-to-advance-ai-engineered-aav-capsids\",\n      \"title\": \"VectorBuilder Partners With Lir Therapeutics to Advance AI-Engineered AAV Capsids - PharmaSource\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2026-08-19\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"CDMO Live Americas Oct 20–21, Boston · Download Agenda →\\nCDMO News\\nVectorBuilder Partners With Lir Therapeutics to Advance AI-Engineered AAV Capsids\\nCOMPANY PROFILE\\nVectorBuilder\\n* VectorBuilder and Lir Therapeutics have entered a strategic collaboration to develop AAV capsids designed for biological performance, manufacturability and scalability.\\n* The companies will combine VectorBuilder’s DeepCap platform with Lir’s AI-powered nAAVigator platform to optimize selected capsids from design through manufacturing assessment.\\nVectorBuilder and Lir Therapeutics have entered a strategic collaboration to develop adeno-associated virus (AAV) capsids that address both biological performance and manufacturing requirements for gene therapy development.\\nThe companies will combine VectorBuilder’s expertise in AAV discovery, capsid engineering, process development and GMP manufacturing with Lir’s nAAVigator artificial intelligence platform.\\nUnder the collaboration, Lir will use its AI-powered nAAVigator platform and laboratory optimization workflow to enhance selected capsids discovered through VectorBuilder’s DeepCap platform.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lirtx.com/post/the-immune-system-doesnt-want-your-gene-therapy-to-work\",\n      \"title\": \"The immune system doesn't want your gene therapy to work\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"This is a problem waiting to be tackled with new data generation methods and whole capsid modelling. As always I'd love to talk with anyone interested in solving this with us.\\n‍\\nThe Good Virus Company\\nLBIC 2 Royal College St London NW1 0NH\\n© 2025 Copyright: Lir Therapeutics\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.bioindustry.org/resource/cell-and-gene-therapy-catapult-invests-in-lir-therapeutics-to-accelerate-development-of-its-ai-driven-aav-design-platform-.html\",\n      \"title\": \"Cell and Gene Therapy Catapult invests in Lir Therapeutics to accelerate development of its AI-driven AAV design platform\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Cell and Gene Therapy Catapult (CGT Catapult) will provide investment to Lir Therapeutics (Lir) from the Innovate UK Cross Catapult Investment Pilot, to accelerate the development of nAAVigator, its AI-driven AAV capsid design platform.\\nThe investment will support Lir in advancing the biological validation of the platform and building the evidence base needed to engage pharma partners and biotech investors.\\nLir has built an AI-driven \\\"lab-in-the-loop\\\" pipeline that designs and selects novel adeno-associated virus (AAV) capsids for use in gene therapies.\\nOnce validated, the platform is intended to enable the streamlined development of bespoke AAV capsid variants tailored to the specific needs of Lir's partners.\\nThe investment will fund biological validation and benchmarking experiments and the generation of additional datasets.\\nKillian Hanlon, CEO of Lir, said:\\nGene therapy is at a crossroads. There are so many diseases affecting millions that could be amenable to treatment with gene therapy, but viral vectors aren’t where we need them to be to do this.\\nThis additional funding is already accelerating development of our platform, and having CGT Catapult’s key expertise on our side is an incredible boon. Overall, this investment represents a springboard opportunity for Lir to advance its pipeline and fuel our commercial development.\\nMatthew Durdy, Chief Executive of CGT Catapult, said:\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lirtx.com/about\",\n      \"title\": \"About\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Lir is an AI viral vector company. Our approach is to revolutionise gene therapy by tackling dose reduction, tissue targeting and immune evasion all at once through state-of-the-art AI modelling and a lab-in-the-loop screening pipeline. Using our nAAVigator® AI platform we're engineering viral vectors for gene therapy, starting with AAV. Our goal is to completely resurface viral vectors, enabling therapies that would be otherwise impossible.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"http://en.vectorbuilder.com/about-us/newsroom.html\",\n      \"title\": \"\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"VectorBuilder and Lir Therapeutics Partner to Advance AAV Capsids Designed for Clinical Success Press Release VectorBuilder and Lir Therapeutics Partner to Advance AAV Capsids Designed for Clinical Success Aug 18, 2026\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://linkedin.com/company/lir-therapeutics\",\n      \"title\": \"Lir Therapeutics\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Lir Therapeutics\\nUsing our nAAVigator AI pipeline we're engineering viral vectors for gene therapy, starting with AAV. Our goal is to completely resurface viral vectors,\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_ea3641f24ffeIOZGZcPjtin4s1\"\n}"
