    "content": "    Capsida Biotherapeutics - Engineering novel AAVs and developing the next generation of gene therapies                                                       \n\n[\n\n![Capsida Logo](https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/capsida-logo-vectorRGB.svg)\n\n](https://capsida.com/)\n\n-   [About](https://capsida.com/about/)\n    -   [Overview](https://capsida.com/about/)\n    -   [Leadership Team](/about/#leadershipsection)\n    -   [Board of Directors](/about/#boardsection)\n    -   [Investors](/about/#investorssection)\n    -   [History](/about/#historysection)\n    -   [Contact](/about/#contactsection)\n-   [Innovation](https://capsida.com/science-innovation/)\n    -   [Capsida Approach](/science-innovation/#approach)\n    -   [CNS](/science-innovation/#cns)\n    -   [Ophthalmology](/science-innovation/#ophthalmology)\n    -   [Capsid Engineering and Preclinical](/science-innovation/#engineering)\n-   [News](https://capsida.com/press-releases/)\n    -   [Press Releases](https://capsida.com/press-releases/)\n    -   [Community Updates](https://capsida.com/community-updates/)\n    -   [Publications](https://capsida.com/publications/)\n-   [Careers](https://capsida.com/careers/)\n    -   [Culture & Benefits](/careers/#culturesection)\n    -   [Current Opportunities](/careers/#opportunitiessection)\n\nCapsid Engineering Preclinical FULLY INTEGRATED \n\n## \n\n# UNLOCKING THE POTENTIAL OF GENE THERAPY FOR ALL\n\n---\n\n##### About\n\nCapsida Biotherapeutics is developing next generation, targeted genetic medicines for rare and more common neurological and ocular diseases across all ages.\n\n[About](/about/ \"Frank Verwiel, M.D.\")\n\n[Innovation](/science-innovation/ \"Frank Verwiel, M.D.\")\n\n---\n\n## Science & Innovation  \n\n### THE CAPSIDA APPROACH  \n\n**Capsida integrates all capabilities needed to surpass the challenges of gene therapy.**\n\n![graphic](https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/CapsidWireframe-blue.png)\n\n### Capsid Engineering and Preclinical\n\nAt Capsida, the scale at which we have engineered capsids is unrivaled. Using our fully industrialized and roboticized screening method, our scientists assess large, diverse engineered capsid libraries for CNS and the eye in non-human primates to quickly identify optimal capsids for disease targets. To quickly advance our mission of providing meaningful therapeutic opportunities for patients with unmet medical need, Capsida characterizes the novel mechanisms of action that enable our engineered capsids to cross biological barriers, optimizes cargo and evolves preclinical disease proof-of-concept in parallel with capsid engineering. Our engineered capsids can be optimized to deliver a broad range of cargo modalities.\n\n[More Information](/science-innovation/ \"Science & Innovation\")\n\n---\n\n##### Team\n\nCapsida’s founding technology originated in the lab of Caltech’s Viviana Gradinaru, Ph.D., Professor of Neurosciences and Biological Engineering at the Tianqiao and Chrissy Chen Institute of Neuroscience. Founded in 2019, Capsida is financed by Versant Ventures and Westlake Village BioPartners and has entered into strategic collaborations with AbbVie, CRISPR Therapeutics, and Lilly’s Gene Therapy Division.\n\nOur leaders have decades of experience in the biopharmaceutical industry and expertise in AAV biology and biologics manufacturing.\n\n[Leadership Team](/about/#leadershipsection \"Team\")\n\n[Board of Directors](/about/#boardsection)\n\n[Investors](/about/#investorssection)\n\n---\n\n##### Partnering\n\n## \n\n### *“Our partnerships with leading global biopharmaceutical companies are key to Capsida achieving its vision of being able to reach more potential patients in need with our enabling genetic medicines.”*\n\n#### Bethany Mancilla, Chief Business Officer\n\nOur goal is to apply the strength of our targeted genetic medicine platform to develop a new generation of transformative therapies. Since our inception, we have entered into strategic collaborations with AbbVie, CRISPR Therapeutics, and Lilly’s Gene Therapy Division.\n\n[Learn More](/partnering/ \"Partnering\")\n\n---\n\n##### News & Events  \n\n### \n\n### CAPSIDA NEWS & EVENTS\n\nMay 12, 2026\n\n### [Capsida to Present Preclinical Data of New Next-Generation, High-Performing Ocular Capsids at ASGCT Annual Meeting](https://capsida.com/capsida-to-present-preclinical-data-of-new-next-generation-high-performing-ocular-capsids-at-asgct-annual-meeting/)\n\nProvides corporate update including appointment of gene therapy expert Romuald Corbau, Ph.D., as Chief Scientific Officer and an update on the CNS programs…\n\nMay 11, 2026\n\n### [CAP-002 Program Update: A Letter to the STXBP1 Community](https://capsida.com/stx-community-letter-5-9-2026/)\n\n![](https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/Capsida_Biotherapeutics_logo@1x-uai-258x102.png)\n\n##### [SEE ALL NEWS & EVENTS >](/press-releases/)\n\n[\n\n![Capsida Logo](https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/capsida-logo-vectorRGB.svg)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n](/)\n\n[](https://twitter.com/CapsidaBio)\n\n[](https://www.linkedin.com/company/69666356)\n\n[info@capsida.com](mailto:info@capsida.com)  \n1300 Rancho Conejo Blvd.  \nThousand Oaks, CA 91320\n\n© 2026 Capsida Biotherapeutics®. All rights reserved – [Privacy Policy](/privacy-policy/) | [Terms of Use](/terms-of-use/)\n\n[](#)\n\n \n\n### Privacy Preference Center\n\n#### Privacy Preferences"
